## 2026-09-04 — Freeze the current screening-engine contract (TICK-245, #167)

## D-043  Product screening is integrated; per-image voting is evaluation-only

The product sends all submitted entrance views in one synchronous Anthropic Messages API call and
returns one integrated result for the four presence criteria. The evaluation-only path retains one
call per image, majority aggregation, and measured flip rates across the eligible 5-7-view corpus;
integrated results must not fabricate per-image counts or flip statistics.

The production and evaluation model is fixed at `claude-sonnet-5`. Reviewable system, single-view,
and integrated instructions live in the committed `src/frontdoor/screening_prompts.json` resource
and are loaded at call time. A successful reply contains exactly the four criteria; every verdict,
integer confidence, and short single-line evidence field is validated as a unit, so malformed
output becomes a recorded error rather than a partial result. The face check remains a separate,
fail-closed privacy audit and never joins the accessibility aggregate.

Spend is reserved before a model call: the public demo retains its $1 run cap and evaluation its
$20 cap. Automated verification uses injected clients and spends $0. Latency is recorded and the
evaluation report computes p95, while the paid observed-latency result remains owned by #62.
Human ground-truth completion remains owned by #302.

